msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:59
msgid ""
"Define two models. In model1, the only degradation mechanism is solvent-"
"diffusion limited SEI growth. model2 includes the same SEI growth mechanism "
"but also includes particle cracking and SEI growth on the cracks. The SEI "
"model is run twice: once on the initial surface and once on the cracks. The "
"equations for SEI on cracks are reported by O'Kane et al. [10] To ensure a "
"fair experiment, particle swelling is enabled in both models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"model1 = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN(\n"
"    {\"SEI\": \"solvent-diffusion limited\", \"particle mechanics\": "
"\"swelling only\"}\n"
")\n"
"model2 = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN(\n"
"    {\n"
"        \"particle mechanics\": \"swelling and cracking\",\n"
"        \"SEI\": \"solvent-diffusion limited\",\n"
"        \"SEI on cracks\": \"true\",\n"
"    }\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:89
msgid ""
"Depending on the parameter set being used, the particle cracking model can "
"require a large number of mesh points inside the particles to be numerically "
"stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"param = pybamm.ParameterValues(\"OKane2022\")\n"
"var_pts = {\n"
"    \"x_n\": 20,  # negative electrode\n"
"    \"x_s\": 20,  # separator\n"
"    \"x_p\": 20,  # positive electrode\n"
"    \"r_n\": 26,  # negative particle\n"
"    \"r_p\": 26,  # positive particle\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:117
msgid ""
"Solve the models with and without cracking. The steps before the 1C "
"discharge make the model more numerically stable so fewer mesh points are "
"required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:-1
msgid "[4]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SEI-on-cracks.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"exp = pybamm.Experiment(\n"
"    [\"Hold at 4.2 V until C/100\", \"Rest for 1 hour\", \"Discharge at 1C "
"until 2.5 V\"]\n"
")\n"
"sim1 = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model1, parameter_values=param, experiment=exp, var_pts=var_pts\n"
")\n"
"sol1 = sim1.solve(calc_esoh=False)\n"
"sim2 = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model2, parameter_values=param, experiment=exp, var_pts=var_pts\n"
")\n"
"sol2 = sim2.solve(calc_esoh=False)"
msgstr ""

